# Gutierrez Joel — design system

Visual reference: `/design` is the human-facing guide (its own copy). This file is the source of tokens and implementation rules.

Spare, editorial portfolio. Craft over decoration. Hierarchy comes from contrast, typography, and whitespace — not shadows, gradients, or chrome noise.

Reuse helpers in `app/components/page-layout.tsx`, `app/components/link-styles.ts`, `app/components/button-styles.ts`, and existing Tailwind patterns. Prefer the documented button kit when a control is needed; do not invent bordered cards or pill chips.

## Principles

Quiet craft. Hierarchy from type, contrast, and space — not decoration.

- Light canvas, dark ink (and the inverse in dark mode)
- Quiet interaction: underline, color shift, focus outline
- Generous space; content-led layouts
- Flat UI plus subtle site noise (`site-noise`); no drop shadows
- Imagery and type carry personality; chrome stays light

## Palette

Monochrome only. Step 0 is lightest; 100 is darkest. Use Tailwind `white`, `neutral-*`, and `black` — never `gray-*`, `zinc-*`, `slate-*`, or hues.

| Step | Class | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | `white` | Canvas light; ink in dark |
| 5 | `neutral-50` | Code surface (light) |
| 10 | `neutral-100` | Image placeholder (light) |
| 20 | `neutral-200` | Borders / dividers (light) |
| 30 | `neutral-300` | Stronger table rules (light) |
| 40 | `neutral-400` | Muted text (dark) |
| 50 | `neutral-500` | Meta, footer, muted text (light) |
| 60 | `neutral-600` | Secondary / description (light); strong border (dark) |
| 70 | `neutral-700` | Quotes / rules (dark) |
| 80 | `neutral-800` | Body (light); borders (dark) |
| 90 | `neutral-900` | Titles, focus, placeholder (dark) |
| 95 | `neutral-950` | Extra Tailwind step; use only if 90 is not enough |
| 100 | `black` | Ink light; canvas dark |

## Roles

Semantic roles map onto the palette. Always pair light and dark. Prefer these tokens over one-off hex.

| Role | Light | Dark |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Canvas | `bg-white` | `dark:bg-black` |
| Ink | `text-black` | `dark:text-white` |
| Body | `text-neutral-800` | `dark:text-neutral-200` |
| Secondary | `text-neutral-600` | `dark:text-neutral-400` |
| Muted | `text-neutral-500` | `dark:text-neutral-400` |
| Borders / dividers | `border-neutral-200` | `dark:border-neutral-800` |
| Stronger table rules | `border-neutral-300` | `dark:border-neutral-600` |
| Image placeholder | `bg-neutral-100` (`imagePlaceholderClassName`) | `dark:bg-neutral-900` |
| Code block surface | `bg-neutral-50` + `border-neutral-200` | `dark:bg-neutral-900` + `dark:border-neutral-900` |
| Selection | black on white | white on black (see `::selection` / `.dark ::selection`) |

Exceptions (not brand accents):

- Syntax highlight tokens in `app/global.css` (`--sh-*`) — semantic only
- Invalid / destructive text if forms appear: `text-red-600` / `dark:text-red-400` — never as a brand accent

## Faces

IBM Plex Sans for reading; IBM Plex Mono for chrome and metadata. Fonts are loaded in `app/layout.tsx`.

- **IBM Plex Sans** — 400, 500, 600 (+ italic). Default body (`font-sans`). No 700.
- **IBM Plex Mono** — 400. Chrome, meta, dates, tables (`font-mono`).

## Scale

One size, one job. Color is a modifier (body / secondary / muted), not a new type style. Titles stay light.

Interactive states (hover, underline, focus) live on components, not here.

| Use | Classes |
| --- | --- |
| Title | `text-3xl font-normal leading-9 tracking-tighter` — `PageHeader` and prose h1 |
| Section title (prose h2) | `text-2xl font-normal tracking-tight` |
| Section title (prose h3 / page) | `text-xl font-normal tracking-tight` |
| Card / list title | `text-base font-medium leading-6 text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200` |
| Lead | `text-xl leading-[1.3] text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200` |
| Body | `text-lg leading-relaxed text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200` — secondary ink for page description |
| Small | `text-sm leading-5 text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400` — body ink for meta values (`metaValueClassName`); secondary for compact lists |
| Label (`metaLabelClassName`) | `font-mono text-xs uppercase leading-4 tracking-wider text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400` |
| Meta (`typeMetaClassName`) | `font-mono text-xs leading-4 text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400` |

## Weights

Page and prose titles stay `font-normal`. Use `font-medium` for card titles and `strong`. Prefer `em` / italic for emphasis in running copy, not bold display weights. Nav links reuse Label metrics; their `neutral-600` idle color is a component state, not a type style.

## Layout

Wide shell, focused reading column, open vertical rhythm between sections.

- Shell: `max-w-site` (1920px) + `px-4 sm:px-6` (`app/layout.tsx`)
- Reading column: `textColumnClassName` / `articleBodyClassName` → `max-w-xl` (centered for articles)
- Home / writing grids: `projectGridClassName` → 1 col, 2 cols from `lg`, `gap-6`
- Major vertical rhythm: `gap-16`, `pageSectionClassName` (`mb-16`)
- `PageHeader` spacing: `section` → `mb-8`, `article` → `mb-12`, `hero` → `mb-16`
- Wide MDX images: `#wide` → `.article-image--wide` (breakout up to ~56rem); see image rule for asset sizes

## Spacing

Use the rhythm the site already uses. Layout is structure; this is the scale.

| Token | Classes | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Micro | `gap-0.5` `gap-1` `gap-2` `gap-3` `gap-4` `px-1` `py-1` | Meta stacks, chrome padding |
| Group | `gap-6` `mb-8` `mt-6` | Header children, section heading, card grids |
| Section | `mb-12` `mb-14` `mb-16` `gap-16` | `PageHeader` article/hero, `pageSectionClassName`, home sections |
| Exceptional | `mt-20` `pb-20` | Long styleguide blocks only |

## Elevation & shape

The interface stays flat. Depth comes from size and placement.

- No meaningful shadows. Depth = size, placement, contrast, borders sparingly
- Site noise texture behind content; sticky nav goes solid white/black when scrolled
- Images: `rounded-none` (global `img` + covers)
- Interactive chrome / focus targets: `rounded-sm`
- Code `pre` / inline `code`: `rounded-lg` (exception for code blocks only)

## Interaction

Shared states for links, buttons, and chrome. No scale, glow, or drop shadow on hover.

| State | Classes | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Hover | `transition-colors` + color shift and/or `underline` | Quiet feedback only |
| Focus | `outline-2 outline-offset-2 outline-neutral-900 dark:outline-neutral-100` | Default interactive chrome |
| Focus (cards) | `outline-2 outline-offset-4 outline-neutral-900 dark:outline-neutral-100` | Project / writing card wrappers |
| Disabled | `opacity-40 pointer-events-none` | Non-interactive controls; pair with `aria-disabled` or `disabled` |
| Selection | `::selection` black on white / white on black | Native text selection |
| Touch | `min-h-11` on small screens | Theme toggle and compact controls; `sm:min-h-0` when desktop can shrink |

## Components

Text-forward links, full-bleed covers, and labeled meta. Prefer helpers over one-off class strings.

| Primitive | Helper | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Chrome link | `chromeLinkClassName` | Mono, uppercase, muted → darker on hover + underline |
| Content / prose link | `.content-link` / `.prose a` | Inherit color, quiet underline, focus with currentColor |
| CTA text link | `ctaLinkClassName` | `text-sm`, muted, underline — default site action |
| Project / writing card | — | Full-bleed `aspect-video` cover, title row, mono meta; no card border or shadow |
| PageHeader / MetaRow | `metaLabelClassName` `metaListClassName` `metaValueClassName` `typeMetaClassName` | Titles and labeled meta grids; `typeMetaClassName` for year / product |
| Theme toggle | — | Text/icon control, `rounded-sm`, touch height on small screens |
| Image overlay | — | Near-opaque white/black scrim; close uses chrome mono styles |

## Buttons

Link = navigation; button = action that does not navigate. Ghost shares the CTA link family. Do not replace portfolio CTAs with primary. Use only these three variants.

| Variant | Helper | Classes | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Primary | `buttonPrimaryClassName` | `inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-sm bg-black px-4 py-2 text-sm leading-5 text-white outline-none transition-colors hover:bg-neutral-800 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-neutral-900 dark:bg-white dark:text-black dark:hover:bg-neutral-200 dark:focus-visible:outline-neutral-100 sm:min-h-0` | Highest-emphasis action on the page |
| Secondary | `buttonSecondaryClassName` | `inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-sm border border-neutral-300 bg-transparent px-4 py-2 text-sm leading-5 text-neutral-800 outline-none transition-colors hover:border-neutral-900 hover:text-neutral-900 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-neutral-900 dark:border-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-200 dark:hover:border-neutral-100 dark:hover:text-neutral-100 dark:focus-visible:outline-neutral-100 sm:min-h-0` | Alternative action |
| Ghost | `buttonGhostClassName` | `inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-sm px-1 py-2 text-sm leading-5 text-neutral-500 underline underline-offset-4 outline-none transition-colors hover:text-neutral-900 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-400 dark:hover:text-neutral-100 dark:focus-visible:outline-neutral-100 sm:min-h-0` | Lowest emphasis; same family as CTA link |
| Disabled | `buttonDisabledClassName` | `opacity-40 pointer-events-none` | Append to any variant; set `disabled` or `aria-disabled` |

## Do's and don'ts

Guardrails that keep the portfolio calm, readable, and consistent across themes.

- Do keep the UI black / white / Neutral gray in both themes
- Do use IBM Plex Sans for reading and IBM Plex Mono for chrome and metadata
- Do preserve the reading column (`max-w-xl`) and spacious section gaps
- Do prefer text links for navigation; use the button kit only for non-navigating actions
- Do keep images square-cornered and covers edge-to-edge in their frame
- Don't introduce colorful gradients, glows, or drop shadows
- Don't use `gray`, `zinc`, or `slate` color scales, or brand hues for UI chrome
- Don't load Plex Sans 700 or ornate / condensed display faces
- Don't crowd the grid or shrink major gaps below the established rhythm
- Don't invent a fourth button variant, bordered card panels, or pill chips
- Don't treat syntax-highlight colors as a general brand palette
